{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   SHARED PROPOSAL STYLESHEET — included by all four templates
   (grid_zero_es/en, off_grid_es/en).

   Before this file existed, each template carried its own ~350-line copy of
   these rules. They drifted: .summary-table was 30% wide in one pair and 45%
   in the other, .tech-wrap existed in one pair and had been flattened out of
   the other, and the flexbox bottom-pinning had only ever been applied to
   Off-Grid. Every fix had to be hand-applied four times (CONTEXT.md records a
   sed pass that clobbered unrelated rules doing exactly this).

   Keep ALL shared rules here. A template should only carry a <style> block of
   its own for something genuinely specific to that system type.

   ── Density scale ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The custom properties below are the single knob for how tight the document
   is. The one-page budget is genuinely tight (see the regression set in
   CONTEXT.md), so if a future proposal overflows, change a variable here once
   rather than hand-tuning individual rules in four files. WeasyPrint 66
   resolves var() normally.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
:root {
  --fs-body:   7pt;    /* intro, client table */
  --fs-table:  6.5pt;  /* standard data tables */
  --fs-fine:   6pt;    /* bank details, chart caption, footer */
  --fs-micro:  5.5pt;  /* notes list, warranty table — floor for legibility */
  --gap-section: 4pt;  /* space above every section heading */
  --gap-table:   3pt;  /* space below every table */
  --pad-cell-y: 1.5pt;
  --pad-cell-x: 3pt;

  --navy:  #1E2D54;
  --green: #4BAE6A;
  --green-border: #3d9a5c;
}

@page {
  size: A4;
  /* The bottom margin is a reserved band for the fixed footer. .footer-wrap
     is position:fixed, so WeasyPrint paints it on every page — reserving the
     space with body padding instead would reserve nothing on the pages
     before the last, and content would render underneath it. */
  margin: 0.75cm 1.2cm 2.7cm 1.2cm;
}

* { box-sizing: border-box; }

body {
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  font-size: var(--fs-body);
  color: #222;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  line-height: 1.15;
}

/* ── BOTTOM-PINNED GENERAL INFO ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* .page-wrap holds everything except the fixed footer, sized to exactly one
   page's content box (A4 841.89pt − top margin 21.26pt − bottom margin
   76.54pt = 744.09pt, see @page above). .flex-spacer sits immediately before
   .bottom-group (Notas/Garantía) and soaks up every remaining point of that
   height, so the general-information block lands flush above the footer
   instead of floating mid-page with a dead gap below it — regardless of how
   much or little content precedes it.

   IMPORTANT — why a spacer div and not `margin-top: auto` on .bottom-group:
   WeasyPrint 66 does not resolve auto margins on flex items. Verified
   directly: with `margin-top:auto` the bottom block renders immediately under
   the preceding content (y≈30pt of a 744pt box) whether or not the container
   has an explicit height. `flex-grow` IS honored, so the spacer is what
   actually does the work here. Do not "simplify" this back to an auto margin.
   (`justify-content: space-between` also works, but would distribute gaps
   between ALL of .page-wrap's children, not just before the bottom group.)

   Degrades safely on a proposal heavy enough to need a 2nd page: flex-grow
   only distributes *free* space, so once content exceeds min-height the
   spacer collapses to zero and layout falls back to plain top-down flow with
   no overlap or clipping.

   NOTE: do not wrap a table in a plain <div> inside .page-wrap. WeasyPrint
   adds ~17pt of phantom height to such a div once it becomes a flex item —
   diagnosed on .tech-wrap, which is why that wrapper no longer exists and
   .tech-table carries its own margin instead. */
.page-wrap {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  min-height: 744pt;
}
.flex-spacer {
  flex-grow: 1;
}

/* ── HEADER ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.header {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: flex-start;
  margin-bottom: 4pt;
}
.header-left { flex: 1; }
.title-cotizacion {
  font-size: 22pt;
  font-weight: bold;
  color: var(--navy);
  line-height: 1;
  /* inline-block so the green rule is exactly as wide as the word, not the
     whole flex column */
  display: inline-block;
  border-bottom: 2.5pt solid var(--green);
  padding-bottom: 2pt;
}
.title-solar {
  display: block;
  font-size: 13pt;
  font-weight: bold;
  color: var(--green);
  line-height: 1.15;
  margin-top: 3pt;
}
.header-logo img {
  height: 40pt;
  display: block;
}

/* ── CLIENT TABLE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.client-table {
  width: 100%;
  border-collapse: collapse;
  margin-bottom: 4pt;
  font-size: var(--fs-body);
}
.client-table td {
  padding: 1.5pt 5pt;
  border: 0.5pt solid #bbb;
}
.client-table .lbl {
  font-weight: bold;
  width: 20%;
  background: #f2f2f2;
  color: #444;
}

/* ── INTRO PARAGRAPH ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.intro {
  font-size: var(--fs-body);
  margin-bottom: 4pt;
  line-height: 1.3;
}

/* ── SECTION TITLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.section-row {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: baseline;
  margin-bottom: 1pt;
  margin-top: var(--gap-section);
}
.section-title {
  font-weight: bold;
  font-size: var(--fs-body);
  color: var(--navy);
}

/* ── STANDARD GREEN TABLE ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.gt {
  width: 100%;
  border-collapse: collapse;
  margin-bottom: var(--gap-table);
  font-size: var(--fs-table);
}
.gt th {
  background: var(--green);
  color: #fff;
  font-weight: bold;
  padding: 2pt var(--pad-cell-x);
  text-align: center;
  vertical-align: middle;
  border: 0.5pt solid var(--green-border);
  line-height: 1.1;
}
.gt td {
  padding: var(--pad-cell-y) var(--pad-cell-x);
  border: 0.5pt solid #ccc;
  text-align: center;
  vertical-align: middle;
}
.gt td.left  { text-align: left; }
.gt td.right { text-align: right; }

/* Italic "Escenario actual" / "Cálculos esperados" label row above the
   billing columns. Grid Zero only, but harmless where unused. */
.calc-label-cell {
  background: #fff;
  border: none;
  padding: 0;
}
.calc-label-text {
  background: #fff;
  color: #555;
  font-weight: normal;
  font-style: italic;
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  text-align: right;
  border: none;
  padding: 0 2pt 1pt 0;
}

/* ── COST TABLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.cost-table { margin-bottom: var(--gap-table); }
.cost-table th.th-item  { width: 27%; text-align: left; }
.cost-table th.th-qty   { width: 10%; }
.cost-table th.th-specs { width: 43%; text-align: left; }
.cost-table th.th-total { width: 20%; }
.cost-table td.td-item  { text-align: left; }
.cost-table td.td-specs { text-align: left; }
.cost-table td.td-total { text-align: right; }
.cost-total td {
  font-weight: bold;
  border-top: 1pt solid #888;
  background: #f9f9f9;
}
.cost-subtotal td { color: #666; }

/* ── TECHNICAL DETAILS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* Full width on both system types. Grid Zero and Off-Grid carry a different
   number of columns (different metrics are meaningful for each), but the
   table itself spans the same width so the two documents read as one family.
   The final column is $/Wp on both — RESUMEN was removed as a section, since
   the contract total it duplicated is already the last row of DETALLES DE
   COSTOS and $/Wp is a technical metric. No wrapper div: see .page-wrap. */
.tech-table {
  width: 100%;
  border-collapse: collapse;
  font-size: var(--fs-table);
  margin-bottom: var(--gap-table);
}
.tech-table th {
  background: var(--green);
  color: #fff;
  font-weight: bold;
  padding: 2pt 4pt;
  text-align: center;
  border: 0.5pt solid var(--green-border);
  line-height: 1.1;
}
.tech-table td {
  padding: var(--pad-cell-y) 4pt;
  border: 0.5pt solid #ccc;
  text-align: center;
}
/* $/Wp closes out the row — tinted so it reads as the commercial summary
   figure rather than just another technical spec. */
.tech-table th.th-wp,
.tech-table td.td-wp {
  border-left: 1pt solid #888;
}
.tech-table td.td-wp {
  font-weight: bold;
  background: #f9f9f9;
}

/* ── NOTES / PAYMENT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.notes-list {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 1pt 0 2pt 0;
  padding: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-micro);
}
.notes-list li::before {
  content: "·  ";
  font-weight: bold;
}
.notes-list li {
  margin-bottom: 0.5pt;
}

/* ── BANK TRANSFER TABLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.bank-table {
  width: 100%;
  border-collapse: collapse;
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  margin-bottom: var(--gap-table);
}
.bank-table th {
  background: var(--green);
  color: #fff;
  font-weight: bold;
  padding: 2pt 5pt;
  text-align: center;
  border: 0.5pt solid var(--green-border);
  width: 50%;
}
.bank-table td {
  padding: 2.5pt 5pt;
  border: 0.5pt solid #ccc;
  vertical-align: top;
  line-height: 1.35;
  width: 50%;
}

/* ── WARRANTY TABLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* font-size and cell padding here are the specific fix for a real overflow
   (CONTEXT.md 2026-07-31): vertical padding, not font size, is what actually
   governs row height in a table this dense. */
.warranty-table {
  width: 68%;
  border-collapse: collapse;
  font-size: var(--fs-micro);
  margin-bottom: var(--gap-table);
}
.warranty-table th {
  background: var(--green);
  color: #fff;
  font-weight: bold;
  padding: 2pt 4pt;
  text-align: center;
  border: 0.5pt solid var(--green-border);
}
.warranty-table td {
  padding: 0.5pt 4pt;
  border: 0.5pt solid #ccc;
  text-align: center;
  vertical-align: middle;
}
.warranty-table td.wleft { text-align: left; }

/* ── MONTHLY COVERAGE CHART ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.coverage-chart {
  max-width: 320pt;
  margin: 2pt auto 1pt auto;
  /* Only the chart image itself is protected from splitting across a page
     boundary — NOT the whole heading+chart+caption group. Protecting the
     whole group meant that if it didn't fit in the space remaining on the
     page, WeasyPrint pushed the entire block to the next page, wasting
     whatever room was left and dragging every section after it down too —
     the cause of a real 1-page proposal ballooning to 2 pages once this
     section moved earlier in the document (CONTEXT.md 2026-07-31). */
  page-break-inside: avoid;
  break-inside: avoid;
}
.coverage-note {
  max-width: 320pt;
  /* Deliberately larger bottom margin than the tight rhythm used everywhere
     else — this is the one intentional gap on the page, marking the
     transition from proposal/design content (Costos, Técnicos, Cobertura) to
     general administrative info (Notas, Garantía), which sits against the
     footer with its own tight rhythm. */
  margin: 0 auto 10pt auto;
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  color: #6B7280;
  line-height: 1.35;
  text-align: center;
}

/* ── PINNED FOOTER ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.footer-wrap {
  position: fixed;
  bottom: -1.95cm;   /* pulled down into the reserved @page bottom margin */
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
}
.footer-card {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  background: var(--navy);
  color: #fff;
  padding: 4pt 7pt;
  page-break-inside: avoid;
  break-inside: avoid;
}
.footer-sig {
  width: 14%;
  text-align: center;
  vertical-align: middle;
}
.footer-sig img {
  height: 28pt;
  display: inline-block;
  vertical-align: middle;
}
.footer-center {
  width: 38%;
  text-align: center;
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  color: #fff;
  padding: 0 5pt;
}
.footer-center .name {
  font-weight: bold;
  font-size: 6.5pt;
  color: #fff;
  margin-bottom: 1pt;
}
.footer-right {
  width: 36%;
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  color: #fff;
  padding-left: 5pt;
  border-left: 0.5pt solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);
}
.footer-right p {
  margin: 0.5pt 0;
}
.footer-right .contact-label {
  font-weight: bold;
  margin-right: 2pt;
  color: #fff;
}
.footer-isotipo {
  width: 12%;
  text-align: center;
  vertical-align: middle;
}
.footer-isotipo img {
  height: 32pt;
  display: inline-block;
  vertical-align: middle;
  opacity: 0.85;
}
.validity {
  text-align: center;
  font-style: italic;
  font-size: 6.5pt;
  color: #555;
  margin-top: 2pt;
}
